# Implementation Plan — FinanceFlow AI (Agentic Financial Operations Platform)

FinanceFlow AI is an Agentic AI-powered financial operations platform built with React, Node.js + Express, MySQL, and Groq API. It automates payment reconciliation, repayment risk assessment, collection follow-ups, document intelligence, and financial analytics through controlled backend tool calling and a strict **Human-in-the-Loop** architecture.

---

## Technical & Architectural Principles

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Normalized Accounting Hierarchy**: The direct redundant foreign keys from `loans` and `companies` to `payment_allocations` have been removed. The precise relational chain is:
> `payments` (1:N) ➔ `payment_allocations` (N:1) ➔ `repayment_schedules` (N:1) ➔ `loans` (N:1) ➔ `companies`.
> `payment_allocations` cleanly links an incoming payment to a specific repayment schedule installment.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Human-in-the-Loop Rule**: AI recommendations do **NOT** directly create final payment allocations. Money is allocated to financial records **ONLY AFTER** explicit human approval (Accountant/Manager/Admin).

> [!NOTE]
> **Decoupled Payment Ingestion & Lifecycle**:
> `Payment API` ➔ `payments (UNMATCHED)` ➔ `Duplicate Check` ➔ `reconciliation_cases` ➔ `Payment Reconciliation AI Agent` ➔ `ai_recommendations` ➔ `Human Verification` ➔ `Approved payment_allocations` ➔ `repayment_schedules Update` ➔ `Payment Status COMPLETED`.

> [!TIP]
> **Learnable Code & Mandatory Documentation**: Every function will feature standardized data-flow top comments (Purpose, Called by, Receives, Data source, Returns, Calls, Error handling), every React component will document props, and every module/table/page will have a dedicated `.md` file with a **Mentor Questions** section.

