## 1. Frozen 12-Table Database ER Diagram & Architecture

The 12-table relational architecture is structured as follows:

```mermaid
erDiagram
    roles ||--o{ users : "governs permissions"
    users ||--o{ audit_logs : "records actions"
    users ||--o{ notifications : "receives alerts"
    users ||--o{ documents : "uploads (uploaded_by)"
    users ||--o{ documents : "approves document (approved_by)"
    companies ||--o{ loans : "borrows"
    companies ||--o{ documents : "owns document"
    loans ||--o{ repayment_schedules : "has installments"
    repayment_schedules ||--o{ payment_allocations : "receives ledger allocation"
    payments ||--o{ payment_allocations : "split into ledger allocations"
    payments ||--o{ reconciliation_cases : "opens investigation case"
    reconciliation_cases ||--o{ ai_recommendations : "generates candidate matches"
    users ||--o{ reconciliation_cases : "assigned to accountant"
    users ||--o{ ai_recommendations : "reviews AI candidate"
    users ||--o{ payment_allocations : "approves allocation"
```

### Table Definitions & Foreign Key Corrected Specifications:

1. `roles` (`id`, `name`, `description`, `created_at`) — Access control levels (`admin`, `accountant`, `manager`, `viewer`).
2. `users` (`id`, `role_id`, `name`, `email`, `password_hash`, `status`, `last_login_at`, timestamps).
3. `companies` (`id`, `company_name`, `registration_number`, `email`, `phone`, `address`, `industry`, `status`, timestamps).
4. `loans` (`id`, `company_id`, `loan_number`, `principal_amount`, `interest_rate`, `total_payable`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `status`, timestamps).
5. `repayment_schedules` (`id`, `loan_id`, `installment_number`, `due_date`, `principal_due`, `interest_due`, `total_due`, `amount_paid`, `amount_pending`, `status`, timestamps).
6. `payments` (`id`, `payment_reference`, `transaction_reference`, `payment_date`, `amount`, `payment_method`, `bank_reference`, `sender_name`, `sender_account`, `raw_description`, `source`, `status`, timestamps).
7. `reconciliation_cases` (`id`, `payment_id`, `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to`, `matched_company_id`, `matched_loan_id`, `matched_repayment_id`, `created_at`, `resolved_at`).
8. `ai_recommendations` (`id`, `reconciliation_case_id`, `agent_name`, `recommended_company_id`, `recommended_loan_id`, `recommended_repayment_id`, `recommended_amount`, `confidence_score`, `reasoning_summary`, `status`, `reviewed_by`, `reviewed_at`, `created_at`).
9. `payment_allocations` (`id`, `payment_id`, `repayment_schedule_id`, `allocated_amount`, `allocation_type`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `created_at`). *(Direct foreign keys to loans/companies removed for clean normalization)*.
10. `documents` (`id`, `company_id`, `loan_id`, `document_type`, `file_name`, `file_url`, `mime_type`, `file_size`, `uploaded_by`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `status`, `created_at`). *(Explicitly supports uploaded_by and nullable approved_by / approved_at)*.
11. `audit_logs` (`id`, `user_id`, `action`, `entity_type`, `entity_id`, `old_value`, `new_value`, `ip_address`, `created_at`).
12. `notifications` (`id`, `user_id`, `type`, `title`, `message`, `reference_type`, `reference_id`, `is_read`, `created_at`).

